# Python Module Import Rules

> file_patterns: ["*.py"]
> description: Standards for Python module imports and initialization

## Environment Initialization
> priority: 1

Rules for environment initialization:
- Execute load_env() at file top
- Ensure project root directory is correctly identified
- All subsequent module imports should be based on this root directory

## Module Independence
Each module should be independently runnable:
- Every core module must have a __main__ test entry point
- Depends on environment initialization
- Must be runnable from project root directory
- Important models should be independently debuggable for AI understanding

## Import Path Rules
Standards for import path usage:
- Use absolute import paths from project root
- Avoid relative imports with . or ..
- Prevent import errors due to module location changes

## Rule Interdependency
These rules are mutually supportive:
- Environment initialization provides foundation for absolute imports
- Absolute imports ensure module independence
- Module independence validates first two rules

## Best Practices
- Always initialize environment before imports
- Keep imports organized and grouped by type
- Use __all__ to define public interfaces
- Document any non-standard import patterns 